Sure — here’s a minimal, clean e-commerce app in a single HTML file with product cards, cart count, and a simple responsive layout.

```
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Minimal E-Commerce</title>

  <style>
    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    body {
      background: #f7f7f7;
      color: #222;
    }

    header {
      background: #fff;
      padding: 20px 8%;
      display: flex;
      justify-content: space-between;
      align-items: center;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
    }

    header h1 {
      font-size: 22px;
    }

    .cart {
      font-size: 16px;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .hero {
      text-align: center;
      padding: 60px 20px;
      background: #111;
      color: white;
    }

    .hero h2 {
      font-size: 40px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }

    .hero p {
      color: #ccc;
    }

    .products {
      padding: 40px 8%;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr));
      gap: 25px;
    }

    .product {
      background: white;
      padding: 15px;
      border-radius: 10px;
      box-shadow: 0 3px 12px #0001;
    }

    .product img {
      width: 100%;
      height: 220px;
      object-fit: cover;
      border-radius: 8px;
    }

    .product h3 {
      margin: 15px 0 8px;
    }

    .price {
      color: #555;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    button {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 10px;
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 6px;
      background: #111;
      color: white;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    button:hover {
      background: #333;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>

  <header>
    <h1>Shop</h1>
    <div class="cart">🛒 Cart: <span id="cart">0</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="hero">
    <h2>Simple. Modern. Yours.</h2>
    <p>Discover our latest products.</p>
  </section>

  <main class="products">

    <div class="product">
      <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/400x300" alt="Product">
      <h3>Classic T-Shirt</h3>
      <p class="price">$25</p>
      <button onclick="addToCart()">Add to Cart</button>
    </div>

    <div class="product">
      <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/400x300" alt="Product">
      <h3>Minimal Sneakers</h3>
      <p class="price">$60</p>
      <button onclick="addToCart()">Add to Cart</button>
    </div>

    <div class="product">
      <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/400x300" alt="Product">
      <h3>Leather Bag</h3>
      <p class="price">$80</p>
      <button onclick="addToCart()">Add to Cart</button>
    </div>

  </main>

  <script>
    let cart = 0;

    function addToCart() {
      cart++;
      document.getElementById("cart").textContent = cart;
    }
  </script>

</body>
</html>
```

Save it as **`index.html`** and open it in your browser.
